From: Tobias Brick <tobiasb@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: exclude the broken GnuTLS PQ timestamp case in Meson

GnuTLS 3.8.13 rejects SHAKE-256 content hashing when generating signed
attributes for an ML-DSA-87 PKCS7 signature. Keep the rest of the test
suite enabled instead of disabling the entire package check section.

Limit the exclusion to Meson's invocation so the installed self-test
still contains the original case for direct diagnosis. Remove this
workaround when the original test passes with a corrected GnuTLS.

Upstream: https://gitlab.com/gnutls/gnutls/-/work_items/1982
Azure Linux: https://dev.azure.com/mariner-org/mariner/_workitems/edit/22607

--- libjcat/meson.build
+++ libjcat/meson.build
@@ -276,3 +276,5 @@
   )
-  test('jcat-self-test', e, env : testdatadirs)
+  test('jcat-self-test', e, env : testdatadirs,
+       args : ['-x', '/jcat/engine{pkcs7-self-signed-pq-gnutls}'],
+  )
 endif
